    "url": "https://cdn.elifesciences.org/articles/108420/elife-108420-video8.mp4",
    "license": "CC BY",
    "description": "Video 8.High-speed imaging of balancer ciliary beating in the aboral organ tilted relative to gravity, illustrating gravity-induced asymmetry.The example on the left shows an aboral organ tilted by approximately 135\u00b0 in the sagittal plane, while the example on the right shows one tilted by approximately 60\u00b0 in the tentacular plane. For each case, the left and right balancer ciliary clusters are displayed separately. Ciliary beating is shown alongside kymographs extracted from two representative clusters. Recordings were acquired at 100 frames per second and are played back at 30 frames per second (0.3\u00d7). A white vertical line overlaid on each kymograph indicates the current frame shown in the video. These examples demonstrate asymmetrical balancer activity consistent with geotactic responses reported by Tamm, 1980.",
